From: Local Z96A hardware validation
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: z96a: enable eMMC HS400

The Z96A Type-C eMMC is a SiliconGo SGM8200C-S32BBG specified for
eMMC 5.1 HS400. The RK3568 DesignWare MMC host supports HS400, and
the board DTS already routes the 8-bit bus and data-strobe pin. Advertise
the device's 1.8-V HS400 capability so the MMC core can select HS400
instead of stopping at HS200.

Do not enable enhanced strobe: the module's HS400 specification does not
by itself establish HS400 Enhanced Strobe support.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
@@ -893,6 +893,7 @@
 &sdhci {
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 	non-removable;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&emmc_bus8 &emmc_clk &emmc_cmd &emmc_datastrobe>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
